    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0225" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/127.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Reinsch.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 19, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 18. Unnecessary to recall Chang to consider our telegram 13th but
                    suggest Chinese Minister Washington be instructed.</p>
                <p>Congress has passed act authorizing leave of absence to Army engineer for service
                    on the board, and, afterward, as chief engineer of Huai River conservancy in
                    service of China.</p>
                <p>Red Cross has asked that Sibert, ex-Panama Canal engineer, be given leave and
                    intends to make him chairman of board.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
